  overview: [
    "Pass `label` (and `required`) to name the field: Android floats the Material 3 in-container label once the list opens or a value fills the field. The field grows with the user's text size, and a label longer than the field truncates on one line clear of the toggle while the field's accessible name stays the whole label. The required star is decorative: a screen reader hears the field as required, from its name (\"Assigned to, required\"). The field fills the parent it is given; a step of its own (`xs`, `lg`, …, with `start` to pin it to the leading edge) or a Container step sets its measure.",
    "On web the field is the Canvas v4 search field: 40px tall (32 small, 48 large) on the sunken fill behind the `field-border` hairline, a leading 16px search glyph, a 400 14px value (13 small) and a 15px chevrons-up-down 10px from its end. The pointer darkens the edge to the subtle ink, and focus rings it in the accent with a 4px halo. The suggestions are a card 6px under the field with a 4px inset and 34px rows; the typed letters are marked in each suggestion on the accent's soft wash, and the chosen suggestion sits on the `muted` wash. Android keeps the Material 3 exposed dropdown: the filled field with its active indicator and drop-down triangle, and the Material menu whose active and chosen rows take the state layer.",
    "In glass mode the suggestion list is a dense-layer glass card under the field (or above it when it fits there); the field, its caret and its toggle stay in place, and picking a suggestion commits the value at once. Solid mode paints the skin's own list.",
    "Arrow Down and Arrow Up open the list and highlight an option while focus stays in the text field. Navigation stops at the first and last matches. Home and End jump to those limits once an option is highlighted; otherwise they retain their text-editing behavior. Enter chooses the highlighted option, Escape closes the list without changing the query, and Tab closes it while moving focus. Typing resets the highlight. Confirming an input-method candidate does not select an option or submit a surrounding Form.",
    "Use `value` with `onValueChange` to control the selection, and use `\"\"` for a controlled empty value. The callback reports selections and clearing the field. `onSelect` remains a selection-only notification. The independent `query`/`onQueryChange` pair controls filtering; choosing an option resets the query to `\"\"`.",
    "The disclosure button has a real target of at least 48dp.",
    "An option can carry a short `detail` (a version, a platform, a count): pass `{ label, detail }` objects in place of strings, and the detail sits at the row's end in the 11px mono face in the subtle ink. Android sets it in the row's type and muted ink. The label is what the query matches and what `value` holds; the row is announced as \"label, detail\".",
  ],
